BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:pokemon-go-wild-area-2026-sendai-japan@pokemon-go-calendar
DTSTAMP:20261023T191227Z
SUMMARY:Pokémon GO Wild Area 2026: Sendai • Tohoku
DTSTART:20261106T010000Z
DTEND:20261108T090000Z
DESCRIPTION:GO Wild Area returns in 2026 with Steel- and Dragon-type Pokém
 on\, the debuts of Gigantamax Duraludon\, Dynamax Dialga\, and Dynamax Pal
 kia\, and powerful mighty Pokémon. Collect GO Safari Balls to help catch 
 these challenging encounters!\nDates: November 6\, 7\, or 8\, 2026 Time: 1
 0:00 a.m. – 6:00 p.m. JST (UTC+9) Location: Sendai\, Japan\, with gamepl
 ay throughout Miyagi Prefecture Ticket: ¥4\,000 (including applicable tax
 es and fees) for one day\nAll event gameplay is exclusive to ticket holder
 s. A standard ticket covers one selected day\; Extra Day add-ons extend el
 igible gameplay to additional days. Gameplay is available only within the 
 event area at the date and time specified on your ticket.\nTicket registra
 tion: Register from September 11 at 8:00 a.m. JST through September 15\, 2
 026\, at 7:59 a.m. JST. Registered Trainers will be notified of their purc
 hase window afterward. Tickets are first come\, first served\, and registr
 ation does not guarantee availability. Read the ticket registration announ
 cement.\n\n▸ Related Events\n\n━━ BONUSES ━━\n▸ Ticket Holder 
 Bonuses\nThe following bonuses apply from 10:00 a.m. to 6:00 p.m. local ti
 me on your ticketed event day.\n• Increased chance to encounter Shiny Po
 kémon\n• 1/2 Hatch Distance for Eggs placed in Incubators during the ev
 ent\n• Up to 10 free Raid Passes per day from Gyms\n• 3/4 Max Particle
  cost for unlocking and powering up Max Moves\n• Daily Max Particle coll
 ection limit increased to 8\,000\n• Increased Max Particles from Power S
 pots and exploration\n• Increased chance of 10 km Eggs from PokéStops a
 nd Gyms\n• Lure Modules last for 2 hours\n• Incense\, excluding Daily 
 Adventure Incense\, lasts for 2 hours\n• 2× Candy for catching Pokémon
 \n• Party Play lasts for 8 hours\n• Chance to encounter mighty Pokémo
 n on Routes\n• 3 GO Snapshot surprise encounters per day\n• Chance to 
 get GO Safari Balls from PokéStops and Gyms\n\n▸ Trading Bonuses\nTicke
 t holders receive these benefits from 12:00 a.m. to 11:59 p.m. local time 
 on their ticketed event day.\n• Up to 6 Special Trades per day\n• 1/2 
 Stardust cost for trades\nShiny encounters are not guaranteed. To use the 
 increased exploration Max Particle bonus\, first collect all available Max
  Particles in the Nearby menu. Adventure Sync can help track exploration d
 istance.\n\n━━ FEATURES ━━\n▸ Gigantamax Duraludon Debuts\nGigan
 tamax Duraludon makes its Pokémon GO debut at Pokémon GO Wild Area! This
  larger-than-life Pokémon will appear in six-star Max Battles during the 
 event.\nTicket-holding Trainers can learn more about Gigantamax Duraludon 
 in the event-exclusive Special Research story. Complete it for an encounte
 r with Gigantamax Duraludon with a Location Background!\nIf you’re lucky
 \, you may encounter a Shiny one!\nPokémon: Gigantamax Duraludon\n\n▸ D
 ynamax Dialga and Dynamax Palkia\nDynamax Dialga and Dynamax Palkia make t
 heir Pokémon GO debuts during GO Wild Area 2026. Both can be Shiny!\nBoth
  Pokémon will appear in Max Battles during the in-person event.\n\n▸ Ma
 champ Wearing a Modern Jacket\nA new costumed Machamp appears in three-sta
 r raids during the event. Lucky Trainers may encounter a Shiny one! Ticket
  holders can also encounter this Machamp as a mighty Pokémon in the wild.
 \n\n▸ Hisuian Sliggoo and Hisuian Goodra Debut\nHisuian Sliggoo and Hisu
 ian Goodra debut at the in-person GO Wild Area events. Ticket holders may 
 find Hisuian Sliggoo in the wild during either habitat hour\, including it
