DESCRIPTION:GO Wild Area returns in 2026 with Steel- and Dragon-type Pokém
 on\, the debuts of Gigantamax Duraludon\, Dynamax Dialga\, and Dynamax Pal
 kia\, and powerful mighty Pokémon. Collect GO Safari Balls to help catch 
 these challenging encounters!\nDates: November 6\, 7\, or 8\, 2026 Time: 1
 0:00 a.m. – 6:00 p.m. local time (UTC−6) Location: Mexico City\, Mexic
 o\, with gameplay throughout the metropolitan area Ticket: MXN$350 (plus a
 pplicable taxes and fees) for one day\nAll event gameplay is exclusive to 
 ticket holders. A standard ticket covers one selected day\; Extra Day add-
 ons extend eligible gameplay to additional days. Gameplay is available onl
 y within the event area at the date and time specified on your ticket.\nTi
 ckets are available on the official event ticket page\, while supplies las
 t.\n\n▸ Related Events\n\n━━ BONUSES ━━\n▸ Ticket Holder Bonus
 es\nThe following bonuses apply from 10:00 a.m. to 6:00 p.m. local time on
  your ticketed event day.\n• Increased chance to encounter Shiny Pokémo
 n\n• 1/2 Hatch Distance for Eggs placed in Incubators during the event\n
 • Up to 10 free Raid Passes per day from Gyms\n• 3/4 Max Particle cost
  for unlocking and powering up Max Moves\n• Daily Max Particle collectio
 n limit increased to 8\,000\n• Increased Max Particles from Power Spots 
 and exploration\n• Increased chance of 10 km Eggs from PokéStops and Gy
 ms\n• Lure Modules last for 2 hours\n• Incense\, excluding Daily Adven
 ture Incense\, lasts for 2 hours\n• 2× Candy for catching Pokémon\n•
  Party Play lasts for 8 hours\n• Chance to encounter mighty Pokémon on 
 Routes\n• 3 GO Snapshot surprise encounters per day\n• Chance to get G
 O Safari Balls from PokéStops and Gyms\n\n▸ Trading Bonuses\nTicket hol
 ders receive these benefits from 12:00 a.m. to 11:59 p.m. local time on th
 eir ticketed event day.\n• Up to 6 Special Trades per day\n• 1/2 Stard
 ust cost for trades\nShiny encounters are not guaranteed. To use the incre
 ased exploration Max Particle bonus\, first collect all available Max Part
 icles in the Nearby menu. Adventure Sync can help track exploration distan
 ce.\n\n━━ FEATURES ━━\n▸ Gigantamax Duraludon Debuts\nGigantamax
  Duraludon makes its Pokémon GO debut at Pokémon GO Wild Area! This larg
 er-than-life Pokémon will appear in six-star Max Battles during the event
 .\nTicket-holding Trainers can learn more about Gigantamax Duraludon in th
 e event-exclusive Special Research story. Complete it for an encounter wit
 h Gigantamax Duraludon with a Location Background!\nIf you’re lucky\, yo
 u may encounter a Shiny one!\nPokémon: Gigantamax Duraludon\n\n▸ Dynama
 x Dialga and Dynamax Palkia\nDynamax Dialga and Dynamax Palkia make their 
 Pokémon GO debuts during GO Wild Area 2026. Both can be Shiny!\nBoth Pok
 émon will appear in Max Battles during the in-person event.\n\n▸ Macham
 p Wearing a Modern Jacket\nA new costumed Machamp appears in three-star ra
 ids during the event. Lucky Trainers may encounter a Shiny one! Ticket hol
 ders can also encounter this Machamp as a mighty Pokémon in the wild.\n\n
 ▸ Hisuian Sliggoo and Hisuian Goodra Debut\nHisuian Sliggoo and Hisuian 
 Goodra debut at the in-person GO Wild Area events. Ticket holders may find
  Hisuian Sliggoo in the wild during either habitat hour\, including its Sh
 iny form.\nUse 100 Goomy Candy to evolve Hisuian Sliggoo into Hisuian Good
 ra.\nPokémon: Hisuian Sliggoo\, Hisuian Goodra\n\n▸ Location Background
 s\nTicket holders who successfully catch Machamp wearing a modern jacket\,
  Dynamax Dialga\, Dynamax Palkia\, Gigantamax Duraludon\, Crowned Sword Za
 cian\, or Crowned Shield Zamazenta from raids or Max Battles have a chance
  to receive a Mexico City Location Background.\nLocation Backgrounds are a
 vailable only from in-person raids and Max Battles\; remote participants c
 annot receive them.\n\n▸ Mighty Latias and Latios\nTicket holders may at
 tract mighty Latias and Latios with Incense\, excluding Daily Adventure In
 cense\, on their ticketed event day. Both can be Shiny and are quick to fl
 ee\, so keep GO Safari Balls ready.\n\n▸ GO Safari Balls\n…\n\n━━ 
 SPAWNS ━━\n▸ Rotating Habitat Hours\nSteel- and Dragon-themed encoun
 ters rotate hourly from 10:00 a.m. to 6:00 p.m. throughout the event area 
 on your ticketed day.\n\n▸ Solid as Steel Hour\n10:00 a.m. to 11:00 a.m.
  12:00 p.m. to 1:00 p.m. 2:00 p.m. to 3:00 p.m. 4:00 p.m. to 5:00 p.m.\nPo
 kémon: Alolan Sandshrew\, Alolan Diglett\, Magnemite\, Shellder\, Onix\, 
