 day\, November 15.\n\n▸ Machamp Wearing a Modern Jacket\nA new costumed 
 Machamp appears in three-star raids during the event. Lucky Trainers may e
 ncounter a Shiny one!\n\n▸ Special Backgrounds\nAfter a successful catch
  from raids or Max Battles\, Machamp wearing a modern jacket\, Dynamax Dia
 lga\, Dynamax Palkia\, Reshiram\, Zekrom\, Kyurem\, and Gigantamax Duralud
 on have a chance to have a new Special Background.\n\n▸ Mighty Latias an
 d Latios\nTicket holders may attract mighty Latias and Latios with Incense
 \, excluding Daily Adventure Incense\, on both event days. Both can be Shi
 ny and are quick to flee\, so keep GO Safari Balls ready.\n\n▸ GO Safari
  Balls\nGO Safari Balls improve the chance of catching Pokémon\, especial
 ly mighty Pokémon. All Trainers can obtain them by spinning PokéStops an
 d Gym Photo Discs during event hours.\nThey can only be used from 10:00 a.
 m. to 6:00 p.m. local time on event days and become inaccessible after the
  event ends.\n\n▸ Supply Balloons\nTicket holders receive hourly Supply 
 Balloons with GO Safari Balls during event hours.\n\n▸ GO Snapshot\, Rou
 tes\, and Party Play\nTake snapshots for surprise encounters with Steel- a
 nd Dragon-type Pokémon. Explore Routes for a chance to find mighty Pokém
 on\, and enjoy Party Play sessions lasting eight hours.\n\n━━ SPAWNS 
 ━━\n▸ Rotating Habitat Hours\nSteel- and Dragon-themed encounters ro
 tate hourly from 10:00 a.m. to 6:00 p.m. on both event days.\n\n▸ Solid 
 as Steel Hour\n10:00 a.m. to 11:00 a.m. 12:00 p.m. to 1:00 p.m. 2:00 p.m. 
 to 3:00 p.m. 4:00 p.m. to 5:00 p.m.\nPokémon: Alolan Sandshrew\, Alolan D
 iglett\, Magnemite\, Shellder\, Onix\, Porygon\, Shuckle\, Skarmory\, Nose
 pass\, Aron\, Beldum\, Piplup\, Shieldon\, Bronzor\, Lucario\, Drilbur\, F
 erroseed\, Klink\, Galarian Stunfisk\, Durant\, Rookidee\, Tinkatink\n\n
 ▸ Daring as Dragons Hour\n11:00 a.m. to 12:00 p.m. 1:00 p.m. to 2:00 p.m
 . 3:00 p.m. to 4:00 p.m. 5:00 p.m. to 6:00 p.m.\nPokémon: Charmander\, Ma
 gikarp\, Dratini\, Gligar\, Trapinch\, Swablu\, Barboach\, Bagon\, Gible\,
  Tynamo\, Axew\, Heatmor\, Deino\, Skrelp\, Tyrunt\, Amaura\, Goomy\, Noib
 at\, Turtonator\, Jangmo-o\, Sizzlipede\, Frigibax\n\n▸ Mighty Pokémon\
 nMighty Pokémon are more likely to have high Attack\, Defense\, and HP ra
 tings and be XL or XXL. They are harder to catch\, and some may be Shiny. 
 GO Safari Balls improve your chances of catching them.\nThe wild mighty Po
 kémon lineup changes each day.\n\n▸ Saturday\, November 14\nPokémon: A
 lolan Exeggutor\, Scizor\, Flygon\, Walrein\, Metagross\, Empoleon\, Magne
 zone\, Conkeldurr\, Haxorus\n\n▸ Sunday\, November 15\nPokémon: Azumari
 ll\, Kingdra\, Aggron\, Ferrothorn\, Hydreigon\, Goodra\, Noivern\, Tinkat
 on\, Clodsire\n\n▸ Incense Encounters\nAll Trainers can attract these mi
 ghty Pokémon on both event days. These encounters exclude Daily Adventure
  Incense.\nPokémon: Alolan Exeggutor\, Azumarill\, Scizor\, Kingdra\, Agg
 ron\, Flygon\, Empoleon\, Magnezone\, Conkeldurr\, Hydreigon\n\n▸ Ticket
  Holder Incense Encounters\nTicket holders can also attract the following 
 Unown on both days.\nPokémon: Unown D\, Unown I\, Unown L\, Unown W\nLuck
 y ticket holders may also encounter these mighty Legendary Pokémon from I
 ncense:\n…\n\n━━ EGGS ━━\n…
URL:https://leekduck.com/events/pokemon-go-wild-area-2026-global/
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:minior-showers-leonids-2026@pokemon-go-calendar
DTSTAMP:20261023T191227Z
SUMMARY:Minior Showers: Leonids 2026
DTSTART;TZID=Europe/Lisbon:20261114T170000
DTEND;TZID=Europe/Lisbon:20261119T235900
DESCRIPTION:Explore by starlight during the Leonids meteor shower for a cha
 nce to encounter Minior in Pokémon GO!\nThis Minior Shower runs from Nove
 mber 14\, 2026 at 5:00 p.m. to November 19\, 2026 at 11:59 p.m. local time
 .\n\n━━ BONUSES ━━\n• Increased Stardust for catching Minior\n
 • Increased chance to encounter Minior from 5:00 p.m. to 9:00 p.m. local
  time each day\n\n━━ FEATURES ━━\n▸ Minior Cores\nMinior has sev
 en different core colors: Red\, Orange\, Yellow\, Green\, Blue\, Indigo\, 
 and Violet. A different core color will debut during each of the six meteo
 r showers listed below. During the Geminids\, one core color will debut in
  the Northern Hemisphere and another in the Southern Hemisphere.\nPokémon
 : Minior (Red Core)\, Minior (Orange Core)\, Minior (Yellow Core)\, Minior
  (Green Core)\, Minior (Blue Core)\, Minior (Indigo Core)\, Minior (Violet
  Core)\nGreen Core Minior debuts during the Orionids. The core colors for 
 the remaining meteor showers have not been announced.\n\n▸ Explore by St
 arlight\nFrom 5:00 p.m. to 9:00 p.m. local time every day during each Mini
 or Shower\, shooting stars will light up the in-game sky. During these hou
 rs\, you’ll have an increased chance of encountering Minior in the wild!
 \n\n▸ Minior’s Form Changes\nMinior begins battles in its Meteor Form.
  When its health drops below 50%\, it changes form and exposes its core.\n
 • Meteor Form: Higher Defense and lower Attack.\n• Core exposed: Highe
 r Attack and lower Defense.\nInitially\, Minior will only be able to chang
 e forms when battling Team GO Rocket\, team leaders\, or in the GO Battle 
 League.\nMinior will not be eligible for the 2027 Latin America Internatio
 nal Championships.\n\n▸ Annual Meteor Shower Schedule\nMinior can appear
  during the following meteor showers each year. Each shower begins at 5:00
  p.m. on its first day and ends at 11:59 p.m. on its last day\, in local t
 ime.\n• Orionids: October 19–24\, 2026\n• Leonids: November 14–19\
 , 2026\n• Geminids: December 11–16\, 2026\n• Eta Aquariids: May 3–
 8\, 2027\n• Southern Delta Aquariids: July 28–August 2\, 2027\n• Per
 seids: August 10–15\, 2027\n\n━━ SPAWNS ━━\n▸ Wild Encounters\
 nYou may encounter Minior in its Meteor Form in the wild during the event.
  You’ll receive 1\,000 Stardust for catching Minior.\nPokémon: Minior (
 Meteor Form)\nMinior encounters are more likely from 5:00 p.m. to 9:00 p.m
 . local time each day.\n\n🔗 https://leekduck.com/events/minior-showers-
 leonids-2026/
URL:https://leekduck.com/events/minior-showers-leonids-2026/
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
