DESCRIPTION:Explore by starlight during the Geminids meteor shower for a ch
 ance to encounter Minior in Pokémon GO!\nThis Minior Shower runs from Dec
 ember 11\, 2026 at 5:00 p.m. to December 16\, 2026 at 11:59 p.m. local tim
 e.\n\n━━ BONUSES ━━\n• Increased Stardust for catching Minior\n
 • Increased chance to encounter Minior from 5:00 p.m. to 9:00 p.m. local
  time each day\n\n━━ FEATURES ━━\n▸ Minior Cores\nMinior has sev
 en different core colors: Red\, Orange\, Yellow\, Green\, Blue\, Indigo\, 
 and Violet. A different core color will debut during each of the six meteo
 r showers listed below. During the Geminids\, one core color will debut in
  the Northern Hemisphere and another in the Southern Hemisphere.\nPokémon
 : Minior (Red Core)\, Minior (Orange Core)\, Minior (Yellow Core)\, Minior
  (Green Core)\, Minior (Blue Core)\, Minior (Indigo Core)\, Minior (Violet
  Core)\nGreen Core Minior debuts during the Orionids. The core colors for 
 the remaining meteor showers have not been announced.\n\n▸ Explore by St
 arlight\nFrom 5:00 p.m. to 9:00 p.m. local time every day during each Mini
 or Shower\, shooting stars will light up the in-game sky. During these hou
 rs\, you’ll have an increased chance of encountering Minior in the wild!
 \n\n▸ Minior’s Form Changes\nMinior begins battles in its Meteor Form.
  When its health drops below 50%\, it changes form and exposes its core.\n
 • Meteor Form: Higher Defense and lower Attack.\n• Core exposed: Highe
 r Attack and lower Defense.\nInitially\, Minior will only be able to chang
 e forms when battling Team GO Rocket\, team leaders\, or in the GO Battle 
 League.\nMinior will not be eligible for the 2027 Latin America Internatio
 nal Championships.\n\n▸ Annual Meteor Shower Schedule\nMinior can appear
  during the following meteor showers each year. Each shower begins at 5:00
  p.m. on its first day and ends at 11:59 p.m. on its last day\, in local t
 ime.\n• Orionids: October 19–24\, 2026\n• Leonids: November 14–19\
 , 2026\n• Geminids: December 11–16\, 2026\n• Eta Aquariids: May 3–
 8\, 2027\n• Southern Delta Aquariids: July 28–August 2\, 2027\n• Per
 seids: August 10–15\, 2027\n\n━━ SPAWNS ━━\n▸ Wild Encounters\
 nYou may encounter Minior in its Meteor Form in the wild during the event.
  You’ll receive 1\,000 Stardust for catching Minior.\nPokémon: Minior (
 Meteor Form)\nMinior encounters are more likely from 5:00 p.m. to 9:00 p.m
 . local time each day.\n\n🔗 https://leekduck.com/events/minior-showers-
 geminids-2026/
URL:https://leekduck.com/events/minior-showers-geminids-2026/
